Add Receiver Adapter
Open your Integration Flow.

Drag and drop the Open Connectors Receiver Adapter to the Receiver lane.
Double-click the adapter to open its configuration.

2. Configure the General Tab
Name: Give a meaningful name for the channel (example: OpenConnector_Receiver).

3. Configure the Connection Tab
3.1 Base URI
Copy the correct Base URI according to your SAP BTP region.

Example:
https://api.openconnectors.ext.int.sap.hana.ondemand.com/elements/api-v2
Paste it into the Base URI field.

3.2 Credential Name
Choose an existing Security Artifact (type: OpenConnector Credentials).
If not created yet, first deploy a User Credentials artifact (Open Connectors type) in Security Material.

3.3 Resource
Click Select next to Resource.
It will show a list of available Resources from your Open Connectors instance.
Choose the API resource you want to access (example: contacts, accounts).

3.4 Method
Select the HTTP method:

GET → Read Data
POST → Create Data
PUT/PATCH → Update Data
DELETE → Delete Data

3.5 Request Format
Choose the format of incoming message:
JSON
XML (only if your payload is in XML, and must use <SwaggerParser> structure).

3.6 Response Format
Choose the format you want in the response:
Same options: JSON or XML.

Do not add manual format converters in the IFlow.

3.7 Query Parameters for Resource (Optional)
If your Resource path has variables or you want to apply filters:

Provide values like:
varname1=value1, varname2=value2
For query parameters:

Example:
${header.query1};${header.query2}
3.8 Page Size and Process in Pages (Optional)
If you expect large results:

Page Size: Enter number of records per page.

Process in Pages: Enable this if using in Looping Process Call.

3.9 Timeout
Set the Timeout (milliseconds) to avoid waiting too long for responses.

Example: 60000 (means 60 seconds).

